# Boots in MAME and POM2, not in AppleWin (AppleWin #1278, open since
# 2024-02-16). The WOZ attached to that issue; source in protected.md.
title phantasie iie protected
  diskii 1 phantasie.woz sha256=a92b0823ffa06ff3f00022c1550f5daf3a807fa973c4ec03a9858a66a8b4d59f
  run 15
  check title
  key SPACE
  run 15
  check menu

# The AppleWin #1005 WOZ with INFO optimal_bit_timing 32 -> 33 and its CRC
# recomputed (recipe in protected.md). Boots only since POM2 honours a
# non-multiple-of-4 cell (STORAGE-016, 2026-11-18): the weak-bit check wants
# $C9 at Y=$2A, and 32 gives $29.
title prisoner2 iie protected
  diskii 1 prisoner2a-t33.woz sha256=09ed6f060c18f88e95cab3990830b65b0128015c9f58ea0dcd570d050cf3cc6a
  run 30
  check title
  run 30
  check resignation-file
  key RETURN
  run 15
  check resignation-code

# The three-way WOZ round of 2026-11-23 (docs/audits/protected-woz-three-way-
# 2026-11-23.md). Mr. Do declares bit timing 29 for tracks that fill a
# revolution at 30; it boots since WozBitTiming.h plays such an image at the
# one-revolution cell. Before, POM2 alone (of POM2, MAME, AppleWin) stayed in
# the boot PROM at $C65E.
title mr-do ii+ protected
  diskii 1 mr-do.woz sha256=5a5c171a2dd077072d3c7aeed5a7fbaff797b6cf9a2c6760df7f91d86820d1ee
  run 30
  check calibrate

# "Ridiculously aggressive copy protection, it will probably not work on your
# emulator" (4am). POM2 reaches the maze on a ][+ and on a ][; MAME's ][
# does not. N answers its Mockingboard question.
title lady-tut ii+ protected
  diskii 1 lady-tut-a.woz sha256=06d2f2c51d0ab3b23d8e878ede127009dde7c4fb6de75411feca8b379b2a9dfb
  run 40
  check mockingboard-question
  key N
  run 30
  check maze

# A WOZ 2.1 FLUX capture (Sirius): boots in POM2 and MAME, not in AppleWin
# (no FLUX support); MAME 0.260 failed it (AppleWin #1255).
title cyclod-flux iie protected flux
  diskii 1 cyclod.woz sha256=7c50a7c9f30469368d1e2e06602a25d37f01c687175cbddab1f15b50a8ef07e0
  run 45
  check running

# The one title of the 2026-11-23 round POM2 alone could not boot. Its loader
# needs a $D7 read twice, which happens only when the platter's speed
# wanders (STORAGE-018, DiskImageWozFlux.cpp): 706 failures in 150 s on a
# steady platter, its title at 30 s with the drift.
title glutton ii+ protected
  diskii 1 glutton.woz sha256=323b32b72abd12ad27cd08943ffee3105713bcc09e5ba2477fdcbe712ab03e3e
  run 30
  check title
  run 30
  check demo
